READ:
  The headline is the FIRST table. loc_best and loc_n_above answer the conversion
  question per neuron: did ANY unit come to carry the relation, and how many?
  n_above reaches 3.5 -- some neuron(s) DO carry it; the conversion happens, and how
  that count moves with P is the encoding-saturation curve in its most direct form.
  loc_best change across the range: -0.012 (rising = the conversion strengthens with P).
  quad clears where pooled linear never does: the structure is present and explicit
  only at second order across the whole range tested.
  Best self-referential scalar across the sweep: eucl (max 0.965). If cos/corr hold up
  where tnorm does not, the discrimination is GEOMETRIC, not amplitude -- which would
  mean saturation is not the limiting factor. Any scalar that looks usable must still
  pass the D120 controls (omit_cue and scramble at chance) before it can be a fitness.
  NOTE: a weak readout failing does NOT mean a GA arm must fail -- selection grips
  variance and would be BUILDING the conversion. Read the sd and max columns.
  Compare PR_state against PR_task: if they track, effective dimensionality is the
  mechanism, and D127's PR-family endpoint is measuring the right thing.

  UNDEVELOPED, RANDOM genomes throughout: no selection, no development, no fitness.
